+# Volt window, hood and cabin refinement — 2026-10-29
+
+The owner supplies the current Volt and a side-profile reference, asking for a corrected front door window, nose and hood, and a slightly lower cabin. V21 straightens the complete front window waist and places its upper leading corner beside the windshield-to-roof junction. The door frame follows that new edge. A tapered transition joins the A-pillar to the cowl without lifting the painted surface through the windshield base. The cabin crown is 35.6 mm lower at car scale. A shallower hood and a 70.4 mm shorter nose remove the previous droop while retaining a continuous, convex bonnet surface.
+
+[Compare matched native Garage views](evidence/volt-reference-refinement-2026-10-29/before-after.html). The reference is inspiration only; all production geometry remains original. No reference photograph is incorporated into game assets.
+
+Requirements: VRF01 straight front-door window and fitted A-pillar/frame; VRF02 shallower hood and refined nose; VRF03 slightly lower cabin; R01 retain the earlier 20 cm windshield advance, corrected rear glass, painted quarter pillars, complete door perimeters, materials, wheels, handling and geometry budgets; Q01 actual-buffer measurements, native evidence, refreshed derived assets and an isolated review checkpoint.
+
+Runtime scope is `game/vehicle/electric_coachwork.gd`. Two new test/review helpers support the change. Actual prepared full/simple buffers pass 18 focused checks. The roof drops 35.590/35.608 mm, hood endpoint pitch falls from 11.442° to 8.686°, and nose overhang decreases 70.400 mm. The front window's previous 27.1 mm model-space departure from its straight lower boundary becomes less than 0.0001 mm. Both windshield longitudinal edges retain their v20 positions. These are geometric measurements, not aerodynamic or physical-device performance claims.
+
+Retained cabin46, bonnet40, rear shape24 and continuity58 pass. Native model/lighting34, actual App Garage/race58, focused racing23 and the preferred owned-source parser pass. The unchanged historical construction test passes 31 of 33 assertions: its two `peak > 1.43` assertions require the former tall roof and fail at the deliberately lowered 1.4028–1.4029 m crown. Its finite buffers/normals, tyre clearance, proportions, budgets, articulation, convex roofline and closed assemblies still pass. The old height assertions and failure receipts remain unchanged; the new comparison requires an actual 3–5 cm reduction from v20. No full-project parser pass is claimed.
+
+Visible full/simple geometry stays at 119238/38224 triangles within 120000/45000; five simplified shadow frames total 3527 triangles. All 421 v21 prepared resources, the Volt Garage template, shadows and 52 native Garage/header/news/livery pictures are rebuilt and imported. Sixteen final clean/synthetic-wear views save in each desktop renderer, plus sixteen matched v20 controls. Review captures include both sides, front, hood, front pillar and rear angles. Owner saves and camera contracts are untouched. The first draft's cowl pinch is retained in `first-preview` and corrected in the final views. Existing App desktop hitches remain in its log and are not a performance pass.
+
+Historical v20 resources and current car configurations are checked for preservation. The task checkpoint substitutes only owned entries in shared manifest baselines so concurrent context is retained. It excludes other tasks' source/configuration changes, current generated build identities, and the main Git index.
+
+[Commands and actual outcomes](evidence/volt-reference-refinement-2026-10-29/commands.json), [report and measurements](evidence/volt-reference-refinement-2026-10-29/report.json), [task-only binary patch](evidence/volt-reference-refinement-2026-10-29/task.patch) and [forward/reverse proof and hashes](evidence/volt-reference-refinement-2026-10-29/checkpoint.json). `run_checks.py` records exact calls through `scripts/dev.ps1`, the pinned engine and an isolated local profile.
+
+Reload/rebuild and owner appearance acceptance remain. No physical-device query/test, APK, owner-save/live/backend mutation, deployment, owner-process restart, or main-index staging/commit/merge was performed. Handling, drag and phone frame-rate improvements are not claimed.
